The numbers is a list of 4, 2, and 3.
The last is the last position of numbers.
The changes is 0.
For every spot from 1 to last.
The previous is item (spot minus 1) of numbers.
The current is item spot of numbers.
The drop is 0.
If current is less than previous, set drop to 1.
If drop is 1, add 1 to changes.
The lowerok is 0.
If spot is 1, set lowerok to 1.
If spot is more than 1 and item (spot minus 2) of numbers is at most current, set lowerok to 1.
If drop is 1 and lowerok is 1, set item (spot minus 1) of numbers to current.
If drop is 1 and lowerok is 0, set item spot of numbers to previous.

If changes is at most 1, show true, otherwise show false.
